:: Heist Landry Approach
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>>
Landry looks past you towards the pub door, then back at you. <<His>> jaw is tight. <<He>> leans in so you can hear <<him>> over the chairs scraping and the talk around you.
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	"We need to talk," <<he>> says. <<He>> guides you to a quiet corner of the pub, away from the hearth and the nearest listeners. "The bank. The gala. I know you were there."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	"Sit down," <<he>> says. "We need to talk about what you've been putting into your body."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	"Sit. Now." <<He>> steers you into a booth and drops into the seat opposite. <<His>> eyes move around the pub before settling on yours.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 1]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 1
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	<<He>> waits for you to say something. When you don't, <<he>> carries on, "That place isn't what you think it is. It isn't some respectable bank throwing fancy parties for rich people.
	It's a laundry. The biggest one in the city. Every dirty money in this town gets cleaned through those accounts, and the pills..."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> glances towards the other drinkers, then lowers <<his>> voice even more.
	<br><br>
	"The X-Change supply? All of it moves through the bank. That's how it spreads so easily. That's why nobody can shut it down."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> fixes you with a hard look. "<span class="elk">The owner</span> controls all of it. And you walked right into <<his>> house."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	"Those premium pills you've been taking. The ones from Briar's stock." <<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "They work, don't they? Maybe too well. That's the point."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> leans in. "Every pill you swallow gives a piece of you to someone. Someone who collects those pieces. They call them '<span class="elk">the master</span>.'
	The pills are a link. A thread. And you've been pulling that thread tighter with every dose."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> gestures vaguely at the world outside the pub. "You feel it, don't you? The way the town has changed. The way things have become stranger, darker.
	<<if $world_corruption_soft gte 50>>You've felt it more than most.<<else>>It's quiet, but it's there.<</if>>."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	"I've been cleaning up after you for months. Your trips to The Gentleman's Club. The blackmail. The leverage you've been gathering."
	<<He>> rubs a hand over <<his>> face. "Do you have any idea how far that trouble has spread?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lowers <<his>> voice to a whisper.
	<br><br>
	"There's a table. Not a real one. <span class="elk">A council</span>. The people who really run this city's underworld. They decide who works, who earns, and who disappears."
	<<He>> holds your gaze. "Your name has come up. Three times now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> lets that sit for a moment before continuing.
	<br><br>
	"I've been keeping you off their list. Calling in favours, burning bridges I can't rebuild. But I'm running out of room."
	<<His>> hands lie flat on the table. "If we don't act soon, they'll come for you. And when the high table decides someone is a problem, that problem stops existing."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask who it is|Heist Landry Owner]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident"))>>
	<<link [[And what's in it for you?|Heist Landry Motive]]>><</link>> | <span class="red">Assertive</span>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Heist Landry Owner
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Who... who is this person?" you ask, your voice smaller than you'd like.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"And who is this person meant to be?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Who is this person, then?" you ask softly.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Who is this person, exactly?" you ask. "Someone I should be impressed by?"
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"So who is this mysterious 'person' then?" you ask. "Someone I should be impressed by?"
<<else>>
	"Who is it?" you ask directly.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Something changes in Landry's face. <<He>> doesn't flinch, but <<his>> eyes tighten, as if the question has touched an old wound.
<br><br>
"Nobody knows. Even the people who work with them directly..." <<he>> says.
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 1>>
	"The high table answers to <<him>>. Every single one of them. When I say 'powerful', I mean they stand above the people who already scare everyone else in this town."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> looks at you steadily. "What I do know is that their business goes deeper than anyone thinks, and they have been running it for a very long time."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Motive
<<effects>>
"And what's in it for you?" you ask, narrowing your eyes. "You're not the selfless type, Landry."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a crooked smile that never reaches <<his>> eyes. "Fair enough. I've got my reasons.
Let's just say their business doesn't leave much room for independent people like me. Every year, the noose gets tighter."
<br><br>
<<He>> pauses, dragging <<his>> thumb once along the rim of <<his>> glass.
<br><br>
"There was a time when this city had room for people like us. That time is running out."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 2
<<effects>>
<<if $xchange.landryGentlemansIntro is 1>>
	"And right now, protecting you is the most dangerous thing I've ever done. So yes, I'd quite like something back for it."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
Landry folds <<his>> arms and leans back, though <<his>> shoulders stay tense.
<br><br>
"I'm not telling you this to scare you. Well," <<he>> pauses, "maybe a little. But the point is, I want to do something about it.
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	And you've already been inside the bank at the top level. That's more access than anyone on my side has ever had."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	And the pills have given you something. A sense for it, maybe. But it's also a chance."
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "blackmail">>
	And we need a distraction big enough that the high table has to look somewhere else. Away from you, away from me."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Approach 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Approach 3
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<He>> leans forward. "Instead of chasing small prizes for a few pills or a bit of cash, we hit the centre of it all. The bank itself."
<br><br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"R-Rob a bank?" you say, breath catching. "I need a bit of time to think about this."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You want to rob a bank," you say slowly. "Right. That is rather more than I was expecting."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Rob a bank?" you murmur. "That's... quite a thing to ask."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Rob a bank," you repeat. "That's bold. Give me a moment."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Rob a bank?" you say. "You do know how to start with the simple jobs, don't you?"
<<else>>
	"Rob a bank? I need some time," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods. "Need time? Well, take the time you need. But don't take too long.
<<if $xchange.blackmail.intro is 1>><span class="red">The high table doesn't wait for anyone</span>.<<else>><span class="elk">Their web gets tighter every day</span>.<</if>>
At the very least, you should hear the details first."
<br><br>
"...Fine." You sigh.
<br><br>
<<link [[Express your doubt|Heist Landry React Insane]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Listen more|Heist Landry React Interested]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay silent|Heist Landry React Silent]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Insane
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Still, this is mad," you stammer. "You can't just rob a bank. Not that bank."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Still, you do realise this sounds completely mad," you say. "That place is a fortress."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Still, this is mad," you say softly. "Truly mad."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Still, this is mad," you say. "That bank is built to stop people like us."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Still, you're out of your mind," you say flatly. "Rob the bank run by the invisible monster. Lovely plan."
<<else>>
	"Still, you're insane," you say. "That bank is a fortress."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry gives a short laugh with no humour in it. "I didn't say it would be easy. I said it would be worth it. There's a difference."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Interested
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"I'm listening," you say carefully.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Go on, then," you say. "Let's hear it properly."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Alright," you say. "Go on."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I'm listening," you say, holding <<his>> gaze.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Alright," you say. "Go on then. Impress me."
<<else>>
	"I'm listening," you say.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods once. "Good. I hoped you'd say that."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry React Silent
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
You say nothing. For a moment, the pub noise feels far away. All you can focus on is Landry and the plan <<he>> is putting in front of you.
<br><br>
Landry watches you for a long moment, reading your silence.
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"I'll take that as 'I think you're an idiot, but I'm still listening.' Fair enough. Hear me out."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Not sold yet? Fine. Hear me out first."
<<else>>
	"I'll take that as 'terrified but curious.' Fair enough. Hear me out."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Explain]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Explain
<<effects>>
"Here's what I know," Landry begins. "The bank has two sides. Upstairs, it's a normal bank. Tellers, accounts, all of that.
But underneath, below all the polished floors and polite smiles, there's a vault system for the real business. Dirty money, pill shipments, and records of every job the master runs in the city."
<br><br>
<<He>> traces an invisible map on the table with <<his>> finger, marking corridors only <<he>> can see.
<br><br>
"The security is serious. Cameras, coded locks, private guards... not the kind who call the police. The kind who make problems disappear."
<br><br>
<<He>> meets your eyes. "But no system is perfect. There are gaps. Shift changes, blind spots, people making mistakes. You just need to know where to look."
<br><br>
<<He>> sits back. "That's the problem. I don't know where to look. I don't have the skills for it. But I know someone who might."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.landryWarned to true>>
<<if $wrenSeen?.length>>
	<<link [[Wren|Heist Landry Wren Known]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Who?|Heist Landry Wren Unknown]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Known
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"You mean Wren, don't you?" you say quietly.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You mean Wren," you say. "That would make sense."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"You mean Wren?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Wren," you say. "That was my guess."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Let me guess. Wren," you say. "The smuggler with the ego problem."
<<else>>
	"Wren," you say. It is not a question.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry raises <<his>> eyebrows, actually surprised. "You know <<nnpc_him "Wren">>? Well. That saves me some trouble."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans forward. "Then you know <<nnpc_hes "Wren">> resourceful, clever, and reckless enough to consider something like this.
Go to <<nnpc_him "Wren">>. Explain what we're planning. If <<nnpc_he "Wren">> agrees to help, come back and we'll sort out the details."
<br><br>
<span class="green"><i>You can now approach Wren about the heist.</i></span><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Unknown
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Who would that be?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Who?" you ask, already trying to place the name.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"And who exactly is that meant to be?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Who?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"A smuggler. Goes by Wren. Mostly works out of the docks. Runs goods through the canals under the city." Landry scratches <<his>> chin.
"Sharp mind. Quick hands. Exactly the sort of person you need for this."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a careful look. "Finding <<nnpc_him "Wren">> might take some effort. <<nnpc_Hes "Wren">> not the type to put up signs."
<br><br>
<<He>> counts the options on <<his>> fingers. "The docks are your best bet. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> sometimes turns up at night near the old warehouses.
Keep your eyes open and your mouth shut, and you'll run into <<nnpc_him "Wren">> eventually."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Wren Unknown 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Unknown 2
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"That's not very specific," you say, unable to keep the nerves from your voice.
	<br><br>
	"It's specific enough," <<he>> replies. "Wren doesn't get found. Wren finds you. Just make sure you're in the right places."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"You do realise that's rather vague," you say.
	<br><br>
	Landry's mouth twitches. "On purpose. Wren likes to be careful."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"That isn't much to go on," you say.
	<br><br>
	"It doesn't need to be," <<he>> says. "Be where Wren works, and Wren will notice you."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Vague," you say. "But workable."
	<br><br>
	Landry nods once. "That's the spirit."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Great. A scavenger hunt," you mutter.
	<br><br>
	Landry smirks. "Think of it as a test. If you can't find one smuggler, you've no business robbing a bank."
<<else>>
	You nod. It's vague, but you've worked with less.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Wren Hint
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"I still haven't managed to find Wren," you admit.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Your smuggler is proving hard to find," you say. "Any better hints?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I still need to find Wren," you say. "Can you narrow it down a bit?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Your smuggler friend is pretty hard to find," you say. "Any better hints?"
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Your smuggler friend is annoyingly hard to find. Got anything better?"
<<else>>
	"I still need to find Wren. Anything else you can tell me?"
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if !$wrenSeen?.length>>
	Landry scratches <<his>> jaw. "Try the canal late in the day. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> moves goods around dusk.
	If the weather's bad, <<nnpc_he "Wren">> sometimes hides near the warehouses on the industrial estate."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> pauses, thinking. "<<nnpc_Hes "Wren">> careful, but not paranoid. Just patient. You'll need to be the same."
<<else>>
	Landry gives you a flat look. "You've met <<nnpc_him "Wren">> before. You know <<nnpc_his "Wren">> usual places.
	Stop overthinking it and go talk to <<nnpc_him "Wren">>."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Mickey Mapping
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Wren sent me," you say. "The mapping is done. <<nnpc_He "Wren">> said to bring it to... your friend."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Wren sent me," you say. "The mapping is finished. I was told your friend should see it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"The mapping is done," you say. "Wren told me to bring it here."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"The mapping's done," you say. "Wren wanted your friend to see it first."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"Special delivery from Wren." You glance at Mickey's door. "Your little hacker friend in?"
<<else>>
	"The mapping is done. Wren said to bring it here for your friend to look at."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Landry nods and knocks twice on Mickey's door. "Got something for you."
<br><br>
The door opens a little. Mickey's eyes peer through the gap. They spot the papers in your hand and open the door wider.
"Are those the bank layouts?"
<br><br>
You nod. They snatch the papers from your hand and disappear back inside. Paper rustles at once, followed by something scraping across a desk.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 2
<<effects>>
A minute passes. Then another. Landry drums <<his>> fingers on the table. Behind the door, paper rustles and Mickey mutters through numbers only they seem to understand.
<br><br>
Mickey's voice comes through the door. "Magnetic strip readers on the service level. Camera system runs on a local network, not hardwired. The vault level..."
<br><br>
A pause. More muttering.
<br><br>
"The vault level has its own power and security loop. Old, but solid."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Mickey Mapping 3
<<effects>>
The door opens again. Mickey leans against the frame.
<br><br>
"I can cut the camera feed on the service level from here. Thirty seconds, timed with your shift change window. That gives you and Wren a clear path to the vault stairs."
They tap the doorframe. "The vault itself, I can't touch from here. That's on you and your skills."
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggery gte 950>>
	"But from what I can see in these layouts, you should be fine," they add. "Good-good."
<<elseif $skulduggery gte 650>>
	"It'll be tight," they say. "But doable, if you don't panic."
<<else>>
	They look at you for a long moment. "You'll want to get better before you go in there. The vault won't be kind."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Mickey retreats and the door clicks shut. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.heistReady to true>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.mickeyPrepDay to Time.days>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.mickeyPrepDays to random(3, 7)>>
Landry turns back to you. "Sounds like we're as ready as we'll ever be. Come talk to me when you want to set a date."
<br><br>
<span class="green"><i>The heist is ready. Talk to Landry to begin.</i></span><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Pub]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Landry>><<person1>><<wearProp "keycard" "black">><<speechresolve>>
You find Landry in <<his>> usual spot, but <<his>> usual calm is gone. The moment <<he>> sees you, <<he>> sits up straight.
<br><br>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"It's done," you say. Your fingers still feel unsteady.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"It's done," you say, slipping into the booth opposite <<him>>.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I did it," you say quietly.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"It's done," you say, meeting <<his>> eyes.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	You set something on the table between you. A plain, dark card. "Miss me?"
<<else>>
	"It's done," you say, sliding into the booth across from <<him>>.
<</if>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved isnot "bratty") and (_speechAttitudeResolved isnot "cruel"))>>
	<br><br>
	You pull the cloned card from the vault terminal and place it on the table. Landry stares at it, then at you.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report 2]]>><<handheldon>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report 2
<<effects>>
"<<pShe>> actually did it," Landry breathes.
<br><br>
For a moment, <<he>> looks truly stunned. Then a grin spreads across <<his>> face, the first real one you've seen from <<him>>.
<br><br>
"You beautiful lunatic. You actually pulled it off!" <<He>> picks up the card, turning it over in <<his>> fingers.
"Do you know what this is? This is a skeleton key. This card can open every account the master runs through that bank. It can track them. Show where the money goes."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey
<<effects>>
A door opens behind you.
<br><br>
Mickey is already halfway across the pub before Landry can react. They move fast, with sharp focus, their eyes fixed on the card in Landry's hand.
They take it in one clean move. Landry barely has time to blink.
<br><br>
"What the..." Landry starts, rising from <<his>> seat to block the nearest tables from seeing.
"Mickey, get back in your room. People can see you."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 2
<<effects>>
Mickey isn't listening. They turn the card over in their hands, holding it up to the dim pub light. Their eyes narrow. Their lips move as if they are reading something you can't see.
<br><br>
"This is the real thing," they mutter. "Do you know what this is?"
<br><br>
"That's what I was just explaining, if you'd..." Landry trails off.
<br><br>
"Shut up." Mickey doesn't even look at <<him>>. They're already walking back towards their room, card in hand. "I'm keeping this."
<br><br>
Landry stares after them, mouth open.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 3
<<effects>>
Mickey pauses at the door to their room and turns back to you. Their expression is different now. Focused, but not unfriendly.
<br><br>
"That card gives direct access. Useless to you as it is. You'd get flagged and frozen within a day." They tap the card against the doorframe.
"But I can use it. In exchange, I will give you <i>a proper card</i>."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 4]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 4
<<effects>><<wearProp "keycard" "black">>
<<if $hbsc.account.level gte 1>>
	"You already have a bank account, yeah? Good-good." They disappear into their room. You hear fast typing. A pause. More typing.
	<br><br>
	They lean back out, holding a different card. Black. Your name is on it.
	<br><br>
	"Your existing account just got raised to <span class="gold">Black tier</span>. No minimum balance, no questions asked.
	As far as the bank's system is concerned, you've always been a Black client." They toss you the card. "Don't thank me. Thank whoever built their security this badly."
<<else>>
	"You don't have a bank account." It's not a question. "Good-good. That actually makes this easier."
	<br><br>
	They disappear into their room. You hear fast typing. A pause. More typing.
	<br><br>
	They lean back out, holding a card. Black. Your name is on it.
	<br><br>
	"<span class="gold">Black tier savings account</span>. Opened, verified, clean as a whistle.
	As far as the bank's system knows, you've been a client for years." They toss you the card. "Don't thank me. Thank whoever built their security this badly."
<</if>>
<<set $hbsc.account.level to 5>><br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Mickey 5]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Mickey 5
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"Thank you," you say, a little dazed.
	<br><br>
	"I just said don't thank me." The door clicks shut. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"Noted," you say, catching the card. "Still, appreciated."
	<br><br>
	Mickey scoff. "Dangerously close to thanks." The door clicks shut. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You catch the card with both hands and look down at it for a second longer than you meant to.
	<br><br>
	Mickey gives a short nod and shuts the door. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Useful," you say, catching the card neatly.
	<br><br>
	"Obviously." Mickey shuts the door. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"So you can do more than lurk behind that door," you say.
	<br><br>
	"And you can do more than pick locks. We're both full of surprises." The door clicks shut. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<<else>>
	You catch the card. Mickey nods once and shuts the door. You hear a complex lock slide into place.
<</if>>
<br><br>
You turn back to Landry. <<He>> still looks like <<hes>> trying to understand what just happened.
<br><br>
"Well," <<he>> says after a moment. "That went differently than I expected." <<He>> shakes <<his>> head and pushes a small wrapped package across the table.
"Got something for you too, as my own <i>thank you</i>. <span class="gold">Premium pills. Five of them.</span> Pulled from a different supply line than Briar."
<<set $world_corruption_hard -= 1>>
<<set $sexStats.pills.pills["X-Change Premium"].owned += 5>>
<<set $xchange.premium.ownedBase to $sexStats.pills.pills["X-Change Premium"].owned>>
<<set $xchange.premium.doseBase to $sexStats.pills.pills["X-Change Premium"].doseTaken>>
<br><br><<earnFeat "Grand Theft Auto">>
<<link [[Tell Landry about the figure you saw|Heist Landry Report Master]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Keep the figure to yourself|Heist Landry Report Silent]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Master
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<if ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy"))>>
	"There was... someone there," you say. "At the end. Watching me."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
	"One more thing," you say. "I saw someone as I was leaving. A figure."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"There was someone there," you say quietly. "Watching me."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I saw someone on the way out," you say. "Watching the whole thing."
<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel"))>>
	"One more thing. I wasn't alone down there. Something was watching me."
<<else>>
	"I saw someone," you say carefully. "As I was leaving. A figure."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"They had..." You struggle for the right word, for a shape that still feels wrong in your head. "Antlers."
<br><br>
The colour drains from Landry's face. <<His>> grin vanishes.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Landry Report Master 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Master 2
<<effects>>
"Antlers." Landry's knuckles whiten around <<his>> glass. "Silver-tipped?"
<br><br>
You nod.
<br><br>
Landry is silent for a long time. When <<he>> speaks again, <<his>> voice is careful, like <<he>> is trying very hard not to sound afraid.
<br><br>
"Then it let you go. You understand that, don't you? You didn't escape. You didn't beat the security. <span class="elk">That</span> watched you take what you took and chose not to stop you.
Which means either you've been given a gift... or you've been given a leash."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask what to do then|Heist Landry Next]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Report Silent
<<effects>>
You decide to keep the figure to yourself. Some things feel too strange once you say them out loud, as if the words might make them worse.
<br><br>
"Clean job. In and out," you say instead.
<br><br>
Landry nods, still grinning. "Beautiful. This changes things. This changes a lot of things." <<He>> settles back, more at ease than you've ever seen <<him>>.
<<He>> raises <<his>> glass. "To the beginning of the end."
<br><br>
But the memory stays with you. The figure. The antlers. The silver-tipped tendrils. The complete stillness.
<span class="navy">You can't shake the feeling that your success was allowed, not earned.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask what comes next|Heist Landry Next]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Landry Next
<<effects>>
"What now?" you ask.
<br><br>
Landry drums <<his>> fingers on the table, thinking.
<br><br>
"Now we use what Mickey pulled from the card. They can start mapping the business. Who gets paid, who moves the pills, where the weak points are."
<<He>> pauses, expression growing serious.
"We're busy, and you... you've done enough for one stretch. Get some rest."
<br><br>
